&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer, Developer Productivity&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build the Nest.js service scaffolding that lets product teams stand up new backend services in our next-generation monorepo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement paved paths, generators, and the platform primitives that make a new service work on day one rather than after a week of wiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the seams that let new services run independently of our existing monolith.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the deployment story for services and web applications on Cloudflare, and the interoperability with our existing AWS and Kubernetes estate managed through Pulumi and Argo CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead migrations of substantial codebases into the monorepo and turn each one into a repeatable recipe rather than a bespoke effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with product teams as platform customers, treating their adoption as the measure of success and their friction as your backlog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the leverage of the whole team by encoding what you learn into tooling, generators and agent-assisted workflows, so the next migration costs less than the last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in engineering citizenship activities such as co-authoring engineering blogs, strengthening our hiring processes, and leading internal hackathon teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
