&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Designer you’ll …&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Agentic CMS experience end-to-end, from early discovery and UX strategy through prototyping, detailed execution, and making sure what we ship is great. Define how enterprise marketing teams author, organize, govern, and publish content across multiple sites and channels — and how that experience holds together as a coherent system, from the visual authoring surface to publishing workflows to localization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for both humans and agents. Build surfaces that work for marketing teams operating at scale and for AI agents querying and composing against structured content, with the right controls, transparency, and trust signals for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think in systems. The CMS touches nearly everything Webflow&#39;s enterprise customers do. Hold a coherent experience model across interconnected surfaces while making individual flows feel simple and obvious.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work upstream. Partner with PMs, engineers, and researchers to shape what gets built. Align on content models, API affordances, and product strategy before pixels get pushed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar — in craft, process, and how you use AI to move faster without sacrificing quality. Present work to cross-functional partners and senior leaders, and bring a point of view on how the CMS connects to the broader Webflow platform.&lt;/li&gt;
